  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="d753b1df-7522-57e4-8ee6-da1298d070e4" activityNameId="0d97b98e-474a-52e6-b83c-c3b3eb6105a7" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Multi-Si wafer, ribbon, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Multi-Si wafer, ribbon, at plant
The reference flow for the life cycle inventory is 1 square metre of wafer surface. The ribbon silicon wafers have a wafer thickness of 250 um. The wafer area is 243cm2, thickness 250 um. The weight is 583 g/m2;
Synonyms: polycrystalline, multi-crystalline, silicon; 
UUID: 1e8b3a01-f432-34b4-94dc-2414479c676a
Sawing and cleaning of wafers. The process data include electricity use, water and working material consumption (e.g. stainless steel for saw-blades, argon gas, hydrofluoric and hydrochloric acid). Production wastes to be treated and process-specific NOx- and waterborne pollutants are considered. No data on other process specific air emissions.
Location: Europe, Western + North America
Technology: Average from 3 specific processes of which one in pilot phase.
Time period: Use of data from an environmental report of a production plant (ca. 3 million wafers per year) and some data from older publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data collection by factory representatives. Environmental report and LCA studies. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_1e8b3a01-f432-34b4-94dc-2414479c676a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
